    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on aggressive baserunning and high-leverage plate appearances. The cornerstone of the lineup is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), our highest-scoring asset, who benefits from a prime matchup against Feltner (xERA 4.69). Given our league\u2019s premium on stolen bases, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Christian Yelich** (73.18) are our clear tactical pillars; both leverage a +13\u201314% platoon edge and exploit the slow delivery of their respective opposing pitchers, creating an elite environment for both counting stats and efficiency. **Kyle Schwarber** (68.21) remains a high-floor anchor, with his xwOBA of .388 suggesting that despite his mid-order constraints, he is ideally positioned to capitalize on the matchup against Phillips.\n\nWhile the depth of our outfield remains impressive, the benching of **Jacob Gonzalez** (50.78) was a difficult call. He sits just outside our \"Strong\" tier, missing the cut primarily due to the daunting presence of Cole on the mound, whose 4.41 xERA isn't nearly as punitive as the standard strikeout risk associated with him, pushing **Jacob Gonzalez** below the efficiency threshold of **Chase Meidroth** (53.91). We are also closely monitoring the status of **Junior Caminero** (62.81); while he is currently projected into the #3 hole against Wrobleski, his official lineup confirmation is pending. Should the order shift downward, we may see a marginal dip in his production, but for now, his raw power profile against a left-handed starter remains a vital component of our offense. Ensure that all daily game caps are monitored, particularly given the aggressive platoon-heavy deployment of **Lars Nootbaar** (57.10) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (58.00).",
